from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd, json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]; R=ROOT/'results/final_evidence'
def tab(d):
 d=d.head(15); c=list(d.columns); return '| '+' | '.join(c)+' |\n| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(c))+' |\n'+'\n'.join('| '+' | '.join(str(v) for v in row)+' |' for row in d.itertuples(index=False,name=None))
def main():
 c=pd.read_csv(R/'claim_ledger.csv'); deep=pd.read_csv(R/'deep_consequence_final.csv'); tf=pd.read_csv(R/'tf_ta_geo_final.csv'); ctx=pd.read_csv(R/'context_final.csv'); rec=pd.read_csv(R/'receiver_supporting_final.csv'); rst=pd.read_csv(R/'restart_claim_final.csv')
 dead=pd.DataFrame([['PL completion/value rho = -0.41','old v2.0','not reproduced','FAIL','changed estimand/eligibility'],['completion and value never agree','old v2.0','not supported as universal','FAIL','completion is insufficient alone, not information-free'],['style-neutral','old v2.0','not supported','FAIL','descriptive associations remain'],['near-perfect zero-shot gaps .001-.004','old v2.0','probability drift remains','FAIL','accepted LOCO calibration'],['universal 40–60 m restart penalty','old v2.0','claim disabled','FAIL','intended-target selection and corrected bands'],['xR-GK universal stable execution skill','old v2.0','exploratory only','EXPLORATORY','split-half evidence limited']],columns=['OLD CLAIM','OLD NUMBER','NEW RESULT','STATUS','WHY IT CHANGED'])
 text='# FINAL SLOAN EVIDENCE LOCK\n\n## 1. Executive scientific verdict\n\nThe central evidence supports ex-ante two-branch goalkeeper distribution valuation. Deep failure consequences are large relative to origin value, while absolute probability scale varies across environments. Intended target geometry adds selected-sample information. Receiver role and identity remain supporting evidence only.\n\n## 2. Final estimands/model\n\nScientific v2.1 definitions, accepted R3.2A calibration/context outputs, canonical xT-GK, and target-identifiable TA-GEO comparisons are admissible.\n\n## 3. Central contribution\n\nGoalkeeper distribution value is an asymmetric expectation: retention probability times retained-action payoff minus failure probability times failure consequence, with origin value surrendered in both branches.\n\n## 4. Major empirical results\n\n'+tab(ctx)+'\n\n## 5. Deep turnover asymmetry\n\n'+tab(deep)+'\n\n## 6. Intended target finding\n\n'+tab(tf)+'\n\nEvery TA result is selected-sample evidence: intended targets are outcome-dependently observed.\n\n## 7. Context/calibration/portability\n\nLOCO supports qualified relative-risk portability, not unchanged probability transfer. Local calibration improves reporting while intervals remain wide.\n\n## 8. Completion — corrected conclusion\n\nCompletion alone is insufficient to value distribution; it is not evidence-free.\n\n## 9. Repeatability/execution\n\nSplit-half residual evidence remains exploratory and is not promoted to stable execution skill.\n\n## 10. Supporting receiver evidence\n\n'+tab(rec)+'\n\nReceiver profile is not a positive main result. Pair identity is appendix/future work only.\n\n## 11. Restart falsification\n\n'+tab(rst)+'\n\nThe historical universal 40–60 m claim is failed/disabled.\n\n## 12. Claims that died\n\n'+tab(dead)+'\n\n## 13. Limitations\n\nReceiver analyses are restricted to target-identifiable actions with outcome-dependent missingness. Event data do not observe all feasible receiver options or checking movement.\n\n## 14. What requires tracking/360\n\nA future option-set model must score every feasible receiver/action j by xR, success value, failure consequence and expected action value.\n\n## 15. Final claim hierarchy\n\nCentral: two-branch xT-GK framework, deep consequence asymmetry, qualified portability. Major: intended geometry and calibration/context. Supporting: receiver role/identity. Appendix/future: profile, pair, #6, long-target, restart conditioning.\n\n## 16. Final figure plan\n\n'+tab(pd.read_csv(R/'figure_plan.csv'))+'\n\n## 17. Abstract fact set\n\n'+tab(pd.DataFrame(json.load(open(R/'abstract_fact_set.json'))))+'\n\n## 18. Exact final thesis\n\n**Scientific thesis (<=50 words):** Goalkeeper distribution should be valued as an asymmetric ex-ante expectation. Deep failure consequences are consistently large relative to origin value, while probability scale varies across environments. Intended target geometry improves selected-sample prediction; receiver identity and tactical option-set claims require stronger data.\n\n**Football/coaching:** Value the decision by both what successful retention enables and what failure concedes.\n\n**Recruitment:** Use risk structure and local calibration as decision support, not transfer-success prediction.\n\n**Opposition/training:** Train release decisions against the consequence of losing deep possession, then validate probabilities in the local environment.\n\n## 19. Explicit DO-NOT-USE list\n\nDo not use receiver-profile, #6, long-target, pair, style-neutral, universal 40–60 m, completion-inversion, or causal transfer-success claims as main-paper numerical evidence.\n'
 (ROOT/'reports/FINAL_SLOAN_EVIDENCE_LOCK.md').write_text(text)
if __name__=='__main__':main()
